SUMMARY:Birds of Peaslee Wildlife Management Area
DESCRIPTION:Join Chris Marks and CMBO Naturalists\, as we explore the birds of Peaslee Wildlife Management Area. Peaslee WMA is an extension of Belleplain State Forest with special areas that attract migrant and breeding songbirds. Get to know some of the very best spots in this wonderful natural area – great for vireos\, tanagers\, warblers and much more! \nWe do not set a firm daily schedule in advance\, leaving us flexible to maximize birding opportunities\, taking advantage of weather conditions\, tides\, and recent bird sightings. \nPREREGISTRATION REQUIRED – Ticket sales end 24hrs before start of program \n\n\nCOST: $20 members\, $25 nonmembers. \nInterested in becoming a member? Please click on the following link to learn more or join: Become a Member today! \nIMPORTANT INFORMATION: \n\n\nWe bird in all weather. Be sure to check the forecast in advance and dress in layers appropriate for prevailing weather conditions. The weather in Cape May can differ considerably from nearby inland areas and may be warmer\, colder\, or windier so it’s best to be over prepared. We may have to bird in the rain\, so please bring your rain gear. \n\n\n\nTRANSPORTATION: Please arrive at the appointed time with a full tank of gas\, as transportation to field sites is by private vehicles.  We may walk up to 1.5 miles\, over generally level\, sometimes muddy or sandy terrain. Some trips involve walks over jetties. \nCANCELLATION: CMBO programs require a minimum number of registrants to run\, five days in advance of the start of the tour but are seldom cancelled. If we do cancel\, due to lack of participation\, severe weather\, or unforeseen circumstances\, we notify all participants in advance\, and all are eligible for a full credit or refund. Participants may cancel without penalty if greater than 30 days in advance. Cancellations 10 to 30 days in advance may be subject to a 25% service charge. No refunds or credits for cancellations less than ten days in advance unless due to health emergencies \n\n\nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://njaudubon.org/event/birds-of-peaslee-wildlife-management-area-4/
LOCATION:Belleplain State Forest\, 1 Henkensifkin Rd\, Woodbine\, NJ\, 08270\, United States
CATEGORIES:Bird Walk,Birding,Cape May Bird Observatory,Cape May Bird Observatory's Northwood Center,Field Trip
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://njaudubon.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/BirdsOfPeaslee_Eventbright_2160x1080.jpg
GEO:39.248546;-74.8428315
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Belleplain State Forest 1 Henkensifkin Rd Woodbine NJ 08270 United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=1 Henkensifkin Rd:geo:-74.8428315,39.248546
END:VEVENT
