SUMMARY:Early Spring Birding at Voorhees & Spruce Run
DESCRIPTION:Join us for birding at two of Hunterdon County’s premier spring migration spots. A variety of habitats can offer a good diversity of bird species including warblers\, vireos\, thrushes and sparrows. We’ll plan to visit portions of Voorhees SP\, Spruce Run SP\, and/or its adjacent wildlife management areas and probably peek at the reservoir to see what shore/waterbirds may be around. Be prepared for a fair amount of walking over fairly flat terrain. Some trails may be wet if it has rained recently so hiking shoes or other footwear you don’t mind getting a little dirty are best. Meet at “Overlook” parking lot on Observatory Road. Led by associate naturalists (and Hunterdon Co. native) Alan Mart. \nMap of the meeting location is here:https://maps.app.goo.gl/Y9WnmcpXYrEM5hw69 \nPRE-REGISTRATION REQUIRED \nCOST: $25 members\, $30 nonmembers. \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://njaudubon.org/event/early-spring-birding-at-voorhees-spruce-run/
LOCATION:Voorhees State Park\, 251 County Rd 513\, Glen Gardner\, NJ\, 08826\, United States
CATEGORIES:All Things Birds,Bird Walk,Birding
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://njaudubon.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Early-Spring-Birding-at-Voorhees-Spruce-Run.jpeg
GEO:40.6960007216;-74.887637733
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Voorhees State Park 251 County Rd 513 Glen Gardner NJ 08826 United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=251 County Rd 513:geo:-74.887637733,40.6960007216
END:VEVENT
